title: The Doctrine of God – Week 7
description: God the Father, the nature and attributes of God: his attributes, the seven Spirits of God, seven things God hates, the names of God, the Godhead and the nature of the Father.
output: lessons/doctrine/doctrine-week-7-doctrine-of-god.html

# Doctrine Week 7. One deck from two old pages: the main page (six sections with tap-to-read cards) and the
# one-page infographic summary, folded in as the closing slide and as extra references where it had more.
# The main page's one SVG (three interlocking gold circles around a single point, with the caption
# "Three Persons, one Godhead...") is rebuilt as the "3 Persons / 1 Godhead" stat pair on the Godhead slide.

=== Introduction
--- The Doctrine of God [title]
overline: Adult Sunday School
heading: The Doctrine of God
sub: God the Father — Week 7 — The Nature and Attributes of God
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- Opening Scripture
big: Genesis 1:26-28

=== I. The Attributes of God
--- The Attributes of God: love, holiness, grace
lead: Tap any reference to read the supporting Scripture in full.
group: Love | | 1 John 4:8; Romans 12:9
group: Holiness | | 1 Peter 1:16
group: Mercy, Compassion, and Grace | | Psalm 86:15; Ephesians 2:8

--- The Attributes of God: wrath, longsuffering, eternal
group: Wrath | | Psalm 7:11; Hebrews 12:29; Romans 1:18; John 3:36
group: Longsuffering | | Psalm 86:15
group: Eternal | | Psalm 90:2; Isaiah 40:28; 1 Timothy 1:17; Revelation 1:8

--- The Attributes of God: just and unchanging
group: Just | | Deuteronomy 32:4; Psalm 89:14; Romans 2:11
group: Immutable, Unchanging | | Malachi 3:6; Hebrews 13:8; James 1:17; Numbers 23:19

--- The Attributes of God: all-powerful, everywhere, all-knowing
group: Omnipotent | | Revelation 19:6; Jeremiah 32:17
group: Omnipresent | | Psalm 139:7-10
group: Omniscient | | Acts 15:18

=== II. The Seven Spirits of God
--- The Seven Spirits of God
lead: [[Revelation 1:4]]; [[Revelation 4:5]] — named in [[Isaiah 11:1-4|Isaiah 11:1–4]]
tile: 1 | The Spirit of the {Lord}
tile: 2 | The Spirit of wisdom
tile: 3 | The Spirit of understanding
tile: 4 | The Spirit of counsel
tile: 5 | The Spirit of might
tile: 6 | The Spirit of knowledge
tile: 7 | The Spirit of the fear of the {Lord}

--- Isaiah 11:1–4
scripture: Isaiah 11:1-4 | mark: spirit of the LORD; spirit of wisdom and understanding; spirit of counsel and might; spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD

=== III. Seven Things God Hates
--- Seven Things God Hates
lead: [[Proverbs 6:16-19|Proverbs 6:16–19]] — things doth the {Lord} hate; seven are an abomination unto Him
tile: 1 | A proud look
tile: 2 | A lying tongue
tile: 3 | Hands that shed innocent blood
tile: 4 | An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations
tile: 5 | Feet that be swift in running to mischief
tile: 6 | A false witness that speaketh lies
tile: 7 | He that soweth discord among brethren

--- Proverbs 6:16–19
scripture: Proverbs 6:16-19 | mark: A proud look; a lying tongue; hands that shed innocent blood; An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations; feet that be swift in running to mischief; A false witness that speaketh lies; he that soweth discord among brethren

=== IV. The Names of God
--- The Names of God
lead: Tap a verse to read it. Each name is shown with its meaning and the verse where it first appears.
table: Name | Meaning and verse
tr: **Elohim** | God as the Creator. A plural name, showing God’s majesty and power [[Genesis 1:1]]
tr: **I AM THAT I AM** | God’s self-existence and eternal nature [[Exodus 3:14]]. The Hebrew here is *’ehyeh ’asher ’ehyeh*; the name YHWH (the Tetragrammaton) is given in [[Exodus 3:15]]
tr: **Almighty God (El Shaddai)** | God as the all-powerful and all-sufficient One [[Genesis 17:1]]
tr: **The LORD (Jehovah)** | God as our provider, covenant keeper, and shepherd [[Psalm 23:1]]
tr: **Jealous (Jehovah Qanna)** | God’s intolerance for competition and demand for exclusive loyalty [[Exodus 34:14]]
tr: **A consuming fire** | God’s holiness and judgment against sin [[Deuteronomy 4:24]]

--- The Names of God, continued
table: Name | Meaning and verse
tr: **God is our refuge and strength (El Ma’oz)** | God as our strong, safe place [[Psalm 46:1]]
tr: **Immanuel** | God with us [[Isaiah 7:14]]
tr: **Lord of lords** | God’s supreme authority over all other rulers and gods [[Deuteronomy 10:17]]
tr: **The living God** | God as the source of all life, in contrast to dead idols [[Jeremiah 10:10]]
tr: **Jesus** | The Savior [[Matthew 1:21]]

=== V. The Godhead / Trinity
--- The Godhead / Trinity
stat: 3 | Persons
stat: 1 | Godhead
center: Three Persons, one Godhead — distinct, co-equal, co-eternal, undivided in essence.

--- The Godhead in Scripture
fig: Three that bear record | 1 John 5:7
fig: Baptizing in the name | Matthew 28:19
fig: Grace, love, and communion | 2 Corinthians 13:14

=== VI. The Nature of the Father
--- The Nature of the Father
lead: His relationship to the Son, and His place over all things
fig: God so loved the world | John 3:16
fig: The Father hath sealed the Son | John 6:27 | The Father as the one who gives authority and approves of the Son’s work

--- The Father over all
fig: One God and Father of all | Ephesians 4:6 | The Father’s position as supreme over all things
fig: Of whom are all things | 1 Corinthians 8:6 | The Father as the ultimate source of all things

=== Summary
--- God the Father at a glance
point: Nature and Attributes | Love, holiness, mercy, compassion and grace, longsuffering, wrath, eternal, just, immutable, omnipotent, omnipresent, omniscient.
point: The Godhead / Trinity | [[1 John 5:7]]; [[Matthew 28:19]]
point: The Seven Spirits of God | The Spirit of the {Lord}, wisdom, understanding, counsel, might, knowledge, and the fear of the {Lord}. [[Revelation 1:4]]; [[Isaiah 11:1-4|Isaiah 11:1–4]]
point: The Names of God | Elohim, I AM THAT I AM, Almighty God, The LORD, Jealous, a consuming fire, God is our refuge and strength, Immanuel, Lord of lords, the living God, Jesus.
point: The Nature of the Father | [[John 3:16]]; [[John 6:27]]; [[Ephesians 4:6]]; [[1 Corinthians 8:6]]
point: Seven Things God Hates | A proud look, a lying tongue, hands that shed innocent blood, an heart that deviseth wicked imaginations, feet that be swift in running to mischief, a false witness that speaketh lies, and he that soweth discord among brethren. [[Proverbs 6:16-19|Proverbs 6:16–19]]
